{% doc %}
  Decides `loading` / `fetchpriority` for an image that MAY sit in the first
  viewport. One place for the ladder that used to be copy-pasted into every
  hero, slide, gallery tile and banner — and drifted (the collection banner
  said `< 2` while everything else said `<= 3`).

  The heuristic is the section's position: an early section is probably on
  screen at load, so its first image loads eagerly, and the very first section
  also gets `fetchpriority="high"`. A position is only a guess — three short
  text sections above a media section leave it above the fold at index 4 — so
  the merchant's `enable_preload_image` checkbox OVERRIDES it: checked forces
  eager + high; unchecked leaves the heuristic in charge, which is exactly what
  every store shipped with.

  Template flow only: `section.index` restarts at 1 per LOCATION, so the first
  section of the footer/header GROUP is also index 1 — the guess therefore
  applies only to sections whose id carries `template--`. Group sections keep
  the lazy default; the checkbox stays the escape hatch.

  Emits `<loading>,<fetchpriority>` — split it on the comma.

  @param {object} [section] - Host section; `section.index` drives the heuristic. Nil → lazy unless `preload`.
  @param {number} [index] - The item's position inside the section (0-based). Only the first item is eager.
  @param {boolean} [preload] - Merchant override (`enable_preload_image`): eager + high whatever the position.

  @example
  {%- liquid
    capture priority
      render 'image-priority', section: section, preload: block.settings.enable_preload_image
    endcapture
    assign priority = priority | split: ','
    assign loading = priority[0]
    assign fetchpriority = priority[1]
  -%}
{% enddoc -%}
{%- liquid
  assign loading = 'lazy'
  assign fetchpriority = 'low'
  assign item = index | default: 0

  if preload
    assign loading = 'eager'
    assign fetchpriority = 'high'
  elsif item == 0 and section.index <= 3 and section.id contains 'template--'
    assign loading = 'eager'
    # Never keep the lazy default's LOW on an eager image: eager + low told
    # Chrome to fetch an on-screen image immediately but queue it behind
    # everything (seen live: a hero at section index 2 shipped exactly that).
    assign fetchpriority = 'auto'
    if section.index == 1
      assign fetchpriority = 'high'
    endif
  endif

  echo loading | append: ',' | append: fetchpriority
-%}
